From cfc7cf4168a229575e3758e1019c6d6b125d5d3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 19:15:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 071/113] rust: drm: framebuffer: add validated shmem scanout
 views

Add framebuffer geometry and reference-counting operations for drivers that retain and inspect scanout buffers outside the atomic callback.

Build borrowed and owned mapping adapters on Lyude Paul's existing shmem::VMap implementation from commit d055768429b3 ("rust: drm: gem: shmem: Add vmap functions"). This patch does not reimplement or claim authorship of that mapping work. The owned form retains the GEM object so a driver can prepare a bounded scanout pool and reuse its mappings across commits.

Constrain both adapters to the driver's exact Rust shmem object type, and reject foreign-device, imported, multiplane, non-linear, block-layout, undersized, and invalid-pitch framebuffers. Apply the framebuffer offset to the returned SysMem view and use checked size arithmetic.

Add KUnit coverage for non-zero offsets, object bounds, plane count, imported objects, and device identity.

Reworked from commit 18546e8725b2 ("rust: drm: kms: add a Framebuffer::vmap() guard") and commit e9a36119bad6 ("rust: drm: framebuffer: add geometry accessors, refcounting and a byte-slice vmap"); the duplicate drm_gem_fb_vmap path is intentionally not carried forward.

